    {
      "id": "vry093h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Sources of Information about Earth's Interior"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth's interior consists of three concentric layers: Crust, Mantle, and Core.",
        "P-waves are the fastest seismic waves and travel through solids, liquids, and gases, whereas S-waves can travel only through solid materials.",
        "Continental crust (SIAL) is composed mainly of Silica and Aluminium and is less dense than Oceanic crust (SIMA), which consists of Silica and Magnesium.",
        "The Asthenosphere located in the upper mantle is semi-fluid and acts as the primary source of magma during volcanic eruptions.",
        "The Core is composed primarily of Nickel and Iron (NIFE), featuring a liquid outer core and a solid inner core."
      ],
      "id": "41y9l0p"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2q0vxij",
      "content": "Direct Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a1jofar",
      "content": "• Deep mining operations."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jj91c3m",
      "content": "• Scientific drilling projects."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aamiuvm",
      "content": "• Volcanic eruptions which bring material from inside the Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jf0ru4z",
      "content": "Indirect Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gvra4fi",
      "content": "• Seismic waves generated by earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p4rbrga",
      "content": "• Study of meteorites."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jexub75",
      "content": "• Gravitational and magnetic field studies."
    },
    {
      "id": "0dy71bg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Seismic Waves"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5sww3n7",
      "content": "• Seismic waves are energy waves generated during earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ev99gah",
      "content": "• They help scientists understand the structure of Earth's interior."
    },
    {
      "id": "edrbuq5",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Wave Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Nature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Characteristics</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>P Waves (Primary)</p>",
            "<p>Compressional (body waves)</p>",
            "<p>Travel through solids, liquids and gases; fastest</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>S Waves (Secondary)</p>",
            "<p>Transverse (body waves)</p>",
            "<p>Travel only through solids</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>R Waves (Surface)</p>",
            "<p>Surface waves</p>",
            "<p>Large amplitude and greater destruction</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>L Waves (Surface)</p>",
            "<p>Surface waves</p>",
            "<p>Cause maximum destruction during earthquakes</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "S-waves can travel only through solid materials.",
      "id": "ydwhfnn"
    },
    {
